# Build context exclusions.
#
# The image gets its secrets from `env_file` (read by the Docker CLI on the
# host) and never from a file copied in, so `.env` must not be in the context
# at all — an accidental `COPY . .` into a layer is how a tunnel token ends up
# in an image.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.freebuff
.omo
.codegraph
.bundle
vendor/bundle

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

logs
tmp
coverage
*.log

# Reported by the container's own healthcheck, not from the host.
bin/*.tmp
